# State Architecture

## Context

app/src/store.ts is a hand-written store, not a library wrapper. createStore returns
{ getState, dispatch, subscribe } and notifies a Set<Listener> after every dispatch.
State is reassigned in exactly one place, app/src/store.ts:29. All domain transitions
live in app/src/reducer.ts, keyed by the Action union in app/src/types.ts.

## Rule

- Change state only via store.dispatch(action) with an action from a creator in app/src/actions.ts.
- Grow behavior in order: new Action variant in app/src/types.ts -> case in reducer.ts -> creator in actions.ts -> colocated *.test.ts.
- Keep reducer(state, action): AppState pure and exhaustive - one case per Action variant, plus the `default:` arm at app/src/reducer.ts:38 returning state unchanged.
- Read via store.getState() and NEVER cache a state object - app/src/store.ts:29 reassigns it on every dispatch; read/write vocabulary lives in state-access.mdc.
- NEVER replace the custom store with a state-management library or hook-based state - it IS the architecture here; banned packages live in dependencies.mdc.
- NEVER call reducer() outside app/src/store.ts and NEVER reassign state anywhere else - store.ts:29 is the single mutation point (editing it: do-not-touch.mdc).

## How to verify

1. `grep -rnE '"[a-z-]*(redux|zustand|mobx|jotai|recoil|immer)"' app/src app/package.json | wc -l` -> prints 0; the quoted form skips the prose at store.ts:4.
2. `grep -rn 'reducer(' app/src --include='*.ts' | grep -v test | wc -l` -> prints 2 (definition reducer.ts:10, call store.ts:29).
3. `grep -cE 'type: "' app/src/types.ts; grep -c 'case "' app/src/reducer.ts` -> two equal numbers (currently 5 and 5).
4. `cd app && npm test && npm run typecheck` -> 20 tests pass in 4 files, then tsc --noEmit reports no errors.
